<title>POLAND: POLISH SUGAR BEET CONTENT DOWN TO 13.8 PCT IN SEPT.</title>
<headline>POLISH SUGAR BEET CONTENT DOWN TO 13.8 PCT IN SEPT.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first Polish beet test this</p>
<p>year on September 2 showed the average sugar content in beets</p>
<p>was 13.78 percent, down from 14.34 percent a year ago, the</p>
<p>Sugar Industry Institute (IPC) said.</p>
<p>The IPC also said the average sugar beet root weight</p>
<p>increased to 732 grammes this year from an average of 664</p>
<p>grammes on September 4, 1995.</p>
<p>			    SEPTEMBER 2   SEPT 4, 1995   OCT 10, 1995</p>
<p>Average sugar content   13.78 pct     14.34 pct	15.98 pct</p>
<p>Average root weight    732 grammes   664 grammes    900 grammes</p>
<p>Root/leaf mass ratio     0.91	    1.35	     1.77</p>
<p>NOTE: The IPC will hold its second and last 1996 sugar beet</p>
<p>test on October 7. Results are expected after October 20.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
